From: Phone OS project <local-candidate>
Subject: freedreno: cache the A504 fragment-coordinate blit shader

Private candidate on the recorded Mesa 26.2.3 / 0016 base. Replaces the
0009 and 0017 diagnostics; do not apply them as well. Not yet qualified.

Use one oversized blit triangle on A504 and a context-owned shader for
matching non-MSAA RGBA8/BGRA8 NEAREST in-bounds 2D blits. Supply the two
independent coordinate transforms through Gallium FS constant buffer 0,
which the existing blitter save/restore path preserves. Retain the tested
arithmetic order, normalized sampler, eligibility and existing writer flush.
Other formats and GPU models retain their shader path. No diagnostic flags,
per-blit shader creation/deletion or activation log. Destroy the cached shader
with the context, following the existing f16 shader lifetime.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_blitter.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_blitter.c
@@ -209,6 +209,97 @@
